Placeholder so the Templates folder is tracked in git.

Drop your template DOCX files here:

  Notice of Hearing.docx   (main template - loaded by default on app start)
  Cover Page.docx          (supporting document)
  Addendum A.docx          (supporting document)
  Addendum B.docx          (supporting document)
  Terms and Conditions.docx (supporting document)
  Signature Page.docx      (supporting document)

The server lists every .docx in this folder via GET /api/templates
and serves them as SFDT via GET /api/templates/{id}. The main template
(Notice of Hearing) is also served via GET /api/template and is loaded
into the editor by default on application start.

Each document may contain its own MERGEFIELDs (e.g. CaseNumber, CaseCaption,
NoticeDate, JudgeName, FirstName, LastName, Address, etc.). When the user
selects supporting documents in the right panel and clicks Generate,
DocIO runs the mail merge on the main template AND on each selected
supporting document using the same case data, then appends the merged
supporting documents to the main one to produce a single consolidated
output document opened in the editor.
